latz(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return a sorted list that has the odd numbers in collatz sequence.\n\n    The Collatz conjecture is a conjecture in mathematics that concerns a sequence defined\n    as follows: start with any positive integer n. Then each term is obtained from the\n    previous term as follows: if the previous term is even, the next term is one half of\n    the previous term. If the previous term is odd, the next term is 3 times the previous\n    term plus 1. The conjecture is that no matter what value of n, the sequence will always reach 1.\n\n    Note:\n        1. Collatz(1) is [1].\n        2. returned list sorted in increasing order.\n\n    For example:\n    get_odd_collatz(5) returns [1, 5] # The collatz sequence for 5 is [5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1], so the odd numbers are only 1, and 5.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    sequence = [n]\n    current = n\n    while current != 1:\n        if current % 2 == 0:\n            current //= 2\n        else:\n            current = (3 * current) + 1\n        sequence.append(current)\n\n    odd_numbers = sorted(list(set(num for num in sequence if num % 2 != 0)))\n    return odd_numbers", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/124": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/124", "solution": "def valid_date(date):\n    \"\"\"Validates a date string against format, month, and day rules.\n    Returns True for a valid date, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not date:\n        return False\n\n    if len(date) != 10:\n        return False\n\n    if date[2] != '-' or date[5] != '-':\n        return False\n\n    month_str = date[0:2]\n    day_str = date[3:5]\n    year_str = date[6:10]\n\n    if not (month_str.isdigit() and day_str.isdigit() and year_str.isdigit()):\n        return False\n\n    month = int(month_str)\n    day = int(day_str)\n\n    if not (1 <